title: "Stop guessing source of block: add explicit `BlockOrigin::StateSync`"
doc:
- audience: Node Dev
  description: |-
    Adds a new `BlockOrigin::StateSync { is_verified: bool }` variant so that blocks
    imported as part of state sync are tagged explicitly, instead of being labelled
    with the generic `BlockOrigin::NetworkInitialSync`.

    Both state-import code paths (the dedicated `StateStrategy` used after warp sync,
    and `ChainSync`'s fast-sync state download) now use `BlockOrigin::StateSync`. The
    relay-chain parachain import queue and the client's notification-gating logic are
    updated to treat `StateSync` the same as the other sync-related origins
    (`WarpSync`, `GapSync`, `NetworkInitialSync`).

crates:
- name: sp-consensus
  bump: major
- name: sc-network-sync
  bump: patch
- name: sc-service
  bump: patch
- name: cumulus-client-consensus-relay-chain
  bump: patch
